# Code owners
#
# This file routes review requests. It records who is asked to review a change
# to a given path, and nothing more. The rules a change lands under are in
# GOVERNANCE.md section 3, and the people who hold maintainer status are in
# MAINTAINERS.md. Where this file and MAINTAINERS.md disagree, MAINTAINERS.md
# is the record and this file is stale.
#
# GOVERNANCE.md section 3.2 requires that a change be reviewed by someone
# other than its author; GOVERNANCE.md section 3 records how that requirement
# applies while the project has a single maintainer. The routing is recorded
# in advance so that adding a second maintainer is a one-line change.
#
# @The-JKR is the GitHub account of A. A. Musse. Ownership is held by named
# accounts rather than by an organisation team, because GOVERNANCE.md section 2
# holds maintainer status with the person, not with an organisation: a team
# entry would route review by organisation membership instead. Adding a
# maintainer is adding an account to these lines and a name to MAINTAINERS.md.

* @The-JKR

# The set GOVERNANCE.md section 3.4 governs. A change to any of these requires
